From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 125hz <nickfugitives@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:10:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] server iOS: opt-in fastsync cells for events and semaphores

Add the server half of fastsync, the in-process event (and optional
semaphore) fast path that Madeira's fork used as its default sync engine.
It is an alternative to madsync, never a companion, and it is off unless
MADEIRA_FASTSYNC selects it.

include/wine/madeira_fastsync.h describes the protocol: every
handle-reachable event gets a 32-byte cell in one table shared by the
server thread and all guest threads of the iOS task, and the cell's packed
{generation, state} word is the event's state. event_sync_signaled(),
_satisfied() and _signal() read and write the cell where they used to read
and write `signaled'; an auto-reset token the server hands to one of its
own waiters is CLAIMED first so no client CAS can take it in between, and
a wait-all that turns out unsatisfiable hands its claims back
(check_wait). add_queue/remove_queue keep a server-waiter count the
client reads before it skips a request. PulseEvent, and a watchdog
request from the client, take one event out of the fast path for good.
With MADEIRA_FASTSYNC_SEM=1 semaphores get the same cell, with the count
in the state half. get_inproc_sync_fd, which has no fd to send on iOS,
answers a cell index; event_op accepts a wake-only and a disable opcode
from the iOS client. A timeout re-checks the objects before it fires
while cells exist, since a client can raise one without a request.

Default behaviour is unchanged: with MADEIRA_FASTSYNC unset (or 0/off),
or whenever the server hands out madsync objects (get_inproc_device_fd()
>= 0, i.e. madeira.cfg inproc-sync = 1, the default), no cell is ever
allocated, every hook takes the existing path, and the timeout re-check
is skipped. Everything is under WINE_IOS.

Validation: compiled for iOS arm64 with the flags of Madeira's
build/wineserver/build.sh against upstream's configured headers; no new
warnings over the unchanged files. The protocol is the fork's, which ran as
its default through the fork's device logs; its host race models are in
the paired Madeira change (build/host-tests/fastsync-*.c).

Playport (decision 0054): carried in patches/wine-unix on the Wine base of
Madeira 8c050d0 (wine-11.19 plus patches/wine-port, Madeira's wine fork at
723d1bf), taken from the madeira-main reference branch's re-port (its
wine-port 0075, the cells on wine-11.19's designated object_ops); it applies
as it is. The server builds event.c, semaphore.c, inproc_sync.c and thread.c
from this tree (build/stages/unix-gaps.sh and Madeira's
build/wineserver/build.sh), so the cells are compiled where they run.
Madsync stays off (patches/madeira-unix 0014); the app sets MADEIRA_FASTSYNC
(MadeiraSession.swift).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: 125hz <nickfugitives@gmail.com>

